{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787116685,"nonce":"+iDD3qWk3dX4ZN9c5bgm8IX4ofc=","title":"**What is wrong.** SPEC §B.8.6 specifies that while an alert is snoozed the Slack card's `Snooze` action flips to `:bell: Unsnooze`, and the §H.4 call-out at `docs/design/SPEC.md:3936-3940` repeats it in the same breath as the colour rule: *\"It gains one field — `*Notifications*\\n:zzz: Snoozed by \u003c@U…\u003e until \u003c!date^…\u003e` — and the `Snooze` action flips to `:bell: Unsnooze`.\"* The field landed in `77886a8`. The action swap did not: the card offers `Snooze` to an operator looking at an alert that is already snoozed.","message":"**The demonstration.** Not run — read, and the reading is narrow. `77886a8` closed `1f7bdd0` against six done-when clauses, none of which named the action swap, and its author recorded the omission deliberately rather than missing it: `v.Actions` is built by `ViewService.actions`, which was outside the fence that ticket was worked under. So the `*Notifications*` field and the action row now disagree about the same fact — one says the alert is quiet until a named moment, the other offers to quieten it again.\n\n**Why it matters.** An action that cannot do anything is worse than an absent one, and this one is worse still because it is not inert: clicking `Snooze` on an already-snoozed alert either extends the snooze silently or is refused, and the operator learns which by doing it in a channel other people are reading. The card's own field has just told them the alert is snoozed, so the button contradicts the line above it — the same class of defect as the flap knobs coaching an operator through a dead damper (`235f347`), where the row said \"this changes nothing\" in one paragraph and offered a tuned number in the next.\n\nIt also leaves §B.8.6 half-implemented with nothing recording that, which is how a spec clause quietly becomes untrue.\n\n**Where.** `internal/notification/service/view.go` (`ViewService.actions`, the builder that must learn the snooze) · `internal/channels/domain/view.go` (`NotificationView`, which since `77886a8` carries the snooze as a fact, so the input is already there) · `internal/channels/render/slack/` (the action row) · `docs/design/SPEC.md:3936-3940` (§H.4's call-out) and §B.8.6 (the binding text) · `77886a8` (the commit that landed the field and recorded this as left undone).\n\n**Scope.** small. The fact is already on the view — `77886a8` put it there — so this is the action builder reading a field that exists, plus a golden.\n\n**Done when.** A snoozed alert's card offers `:bell: Unsnooze` and not `Snooze`, an unsnoozed one is unchanged, and a golden pins both so the pair cannot drift apart again. The action's `value` carries whatever the unsnooze handler needs to identify the alert. ⛔ The colour and emoji stay as they are: `1f7bdd0` refused \"neither card is firing-red\" with citations, and §P-17's golden now proves a snoozed critical still renders `#a30200` — this ticket does not reopen that.","files":null}]}